-- title:
--   Surjectivity of the depth component map for J_H(M) at p ∥ M
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a level $M$ with $p \mid M$ and $p^2 \nmid M$, and a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ containing every unit whose image in $(\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$ is $1$; let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ in which $p$ is a non-unit, with residue field $\kappa$ of characteristic $p$ and algebraically closed. Write $F$ for `xHFunctionFieldBar M H`, the base change to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of the level-$M$ function field inside Laurent series, $F'$ for the corresponding field at level $M/p$ with the subgroup `infSubgroup p M H hpM` (the image of $H$ in $(\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$), and $\mathrm{Fb}$ for the characteristic-$p$ $q$-expansion function field of `ΓN p M H hpM` over $\kappa$. The data are: a $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-algebra automorphism $\theta$ of $F$ commuting with the arithmetic Galois action of $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$; an integral $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-algebra map $\alpha : F' \to F$ which is the identity on the underlying Laurent series, with $\theta \circ \alpha$ integral as well; a unit $pb$ of $\mathbb{Z}/(M/p)$ reducing to $p$, and $\delta$ the action on places of $\mathrm{Fb}$ of the automorphism `diamondActionModL` attached to a $\Gamma_0(M/p)$-lift of $pb$; a finite set $SS$ of pairs of places of $\mathrm{Fb}$ whose members are exactly the supersingular node pairs (second entry supersingular, first entry its mod-$p$ Frobenius image); a place specialisation $Psp$ for these data at $A$ and a prolongation datum $Rpd = (R_1,R_2)$ for $Psp$ and $\theta$. The hypotheses assumed are that every supersingular place and its Frobenius image are $\delta$-fixed, the type dichotomy for $(\alpha,\theta\circ\alpha,\delta)$, the model law, the order law at fixed places, and the regularity and node-value laws at $SS$; further, widths $e : SS \to \mathbb{N}$ with $e(s) > 0$, and for each $s \in SS$ an annulus of $F$ over $A$ whose domain is exactly the set of places $W$ with $\mathrm{reduceFst}\,W = s_1$ that are strict neither of the first nor of the second kind, whose modulus is $p^{e(s)}$ times a unit of $A$, whose parameter is fixed by the inertia subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb{Q}$, with the parameter lying in the integers of $R_2$ with non-zero residue of order $1$ at $s_2$, the flipped element $\mathrm{modulus} \cdot \mathrm{param}^{-1}$ lying in the integers of $R_1$ with residue of order $1$ at $s_1$, and the two accompanying unit-evaluation clauses for functions of order zero on the annulus. Finally, a weight $\mathrm{depth}$ on places of $F$ such that every annulus satisfying that list of clauses at $s$ obeys `AnnulusDepthLawInf`, namely $v_A(V.\mathrm{evalAt}(\mathrm{modulus}\cdot\mathrm{param}^{-1})) = v_A(p)^{\mathrm{depth}(V)}$ at all inertia-fixed places $V$ over $s_1$; an additive map $\mathrm{comp}$ from the inertia invariants of $J_H(M)$ to `componentGroup e` satisfying the depth component law for $(\alpha, \theta\circ\alpha, \delta, SS, e, \mathrm{depth})$; and the existence of inertia-fixed places of $F$ that are strict of the first, respectively of the second, kind. Under all these, $\mathrm{comp}$ is surjective.
--
--   This is the surjectivity half of the computation of Raynaud's component map for the Néron model of $J_H(M)$ at a prime exactly dividing the level: the component group, presented as the dual character lattice modulo the image of the Gram map of the widths $e$, is generated by the vertex classes, and the depth-reading map hits each of them. It feeds the packaging theorem which produces the depth function, the component map and its laws together with surjectivity.
